dict(when='2026-10-30 13:32',who='Marc Caputo, Axios, relayed by Jake Johnston (@JakobJohnston)',where='Axios, Washington',url='https://www.axios.com/2026/10/30/trump-bukele-haiti-troop-surge',text='Axios reports that Bukele called Trump on Tuesday to make sure Washington would not object to the surge, and Trump told him, "Do what you have to do," warning that "it might get messy." Up to 2,000 troops are going in and the number "could double or triple"; Haiti approved a bilateral agreement on Wednesday; the force works alongside the Gang Suppression Force and Erik Prince\'s Vectus Global. Axios says Haiti "may be a test case" for Bukele and Prince "to act as public-private proxies for U.S. muscle." One source says Rubio wants Haiti "off the radar"; another says US requests for drones and transport planes were officially turned down and that Colombia may serve as an unofficial go-between. Rep. Brian Mast: "I hope the mission is revenge, retribution and destruction of the gangs."',evidence='Sources briefed on the call, not named; Mast named',other='The Haitian Times relays the report and adds that the terms of the bilateral agreement have not been made public.',links=[['Johnston on X', 'https://x.com/JakobJohnston/status/2116131066838737350'], ['Johnston on the "proxies" line', 'https://x.com/JakobJohnston/status/2116134308381446359'], ['The Haitian Times, 30 Oct', 'https://haitiantimes.com/2026/10/30/do-what-you-have-to-do-trump-backs-bukeles-troop-deployment-to-haiti/']]),
