dict(when='2026-10-30 01:55',who='Jacqueline Charles, Miami Herald',where='Miami Herald, Port-au-Prince and San Salvador',url='https://www.miamiherald.com/news/nation-world/world/americas/haiti/article317841422.html',text='Bukele addressed Haitians in a video message: "This is not an operation against the Haitian people." The Herald reports that at least one airlift was flown by a US military aircraft, that Colombia helped with logistics, that more than a dozen flights have landed, and that no signed agreement with Haiti has been made public.',evidence="Bukele's own video; the reporter's sources, not named",other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-30 01:24',who='Jacqueline Charles, Miami Herald',where='Miami Herald, Port-au-Prince and the lower Artibonite',url='https://www.miamiherald.com/news/nation-world/world/americas/haiti/article317826718.html',text='The Salvadoran contingent has grown from a 125-member aviation unit to at least 2,000 troops (special forces, marines, infantry and support) and was expected to reach about 2,500 by the end of Thursday, against 2,526 for the whole Gang Suppression Force before the surge. Most of the Salvadorans have not had the force\'s two-week human rights course, and sources say no status-of-forces agreement has been signed. The Herald counts five security structures now at work: the Haitian police, the Haitian army, the Gang Suppression Force, a drone task force using contractors linked to Erik Prince, and the Salvadorans. The troops stay at a camp near the US Embassy. Former defense minister Jean Dorneval: "They need to have a legal framework or else they are mercenaries." Vanda Felbab-Brown of Brookings warns about the rules of engagement and the civilian toll of drone strikes. In the lower Artibonite, Bertide Horace welcomes Bukele while Gran Grif has pressed an offensive on Petite Rivière since 19 Oct, with bodies in the river and armed men in the town center. Jean Gilles Bernard Camille says a Salvadoran helicopter was nearly shot down. Doctors Without Borders has suspended its mobile clinics.',evidence='Named people quoted; several sources not named',other='Not yet reported by others: the near shootdown of a helicopter and the lack of human rights training.',links=[]),
