dict(when='2026-10-29 23:33',who='Radio Télé Confiance (@RTConfiance), relayed by Jacqueline Charles',where='X, Santo, Croix-des-Bouquets',url='https://x.com/RTConfiance/status/2115920093846667310',text='A resident of Santo, not named, says Chen Mechan is forcing youths over 17 to join it, threatening those who refuse with death, and charging up to 1,500 gourdes to residents who want to leave. Its checkpoints run from Santo 9 to Santo 17 and as far as Chada. The station says police pressure is stepping up, with explosions it attributes to kamikaze drones and gang members killed or wounded, and "no verifiable toll."',evidence='Anonymous resident; photos',other='Not yet reported by others.',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 23:24',who='@Corvington_CM',where='X, Port-au-Prince',url='https://x.com/Corvington_CM/status/2115917627579322394',text="The account compares the two governments' statements: the Haitian Prime Minister's office says the Salvadorans act within the Gang Suppression Force and must respect the Haitian state, while El Salvador's foreign ministry does not mention the multinational mission. Neither says who commands the troops. It notes that a law passed in El Salvador on 29 Sep authorized Bukele to send only about 78 soldiers.",evidence='Reading of the two official statements',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 23:14',who='Nayib Bukele (@nayibbukele), President of El Salvador',where='X, video in Haitian Creole with Spanish',url='https://x.com/nayibbukele/status/2115915319134855447',text='In a message in Haitian Creole: "People of Haiti, we have almost finished deploying our soldiers and our equipment on Haitian soil. This is not an operation against the Haitian people, nor an invasion of Haiti. We are not a great power. We have no interest in dominating the Haitian people or in taking Haiti\'s wealth." About 3.1 million views.',evidence='Post and video from the president himself',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 22:01',who='Rolfy Martínez (@RolfyMartinez), relaying Lanmò San Jou of 400 Mawozo',where='X, a church, place not shown',url='https://x.com/RolfyMartinez/status/2115896728553742482',text='Video in which the 400 Mawozo leader visits a church. Martínez: "Judge for yourself, maybe he is asking for forgiveness."',evidence="Video from the gang leader's social media; no date or place we can check",other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 21:44',who='Paolo Luers, Salvadoran columnist (@paololuers)',where='Column, San Salvador, Spanish',url='https://x.com/paololuers/status/2115892660657360980',text='Column "Con Bukele, se agudiza la crisis en Haití" (With Bukele, the crisis in Haiti deepens): many actors work without a clear framework, the Gang Suppression Force, the Haitian police, Vectus Global\'s private contractors and the Salvadoran reinforcement, whose place is vague. It carries Romain Le Cour\'s questions in Spanish, says Bukele\'s documented closeness to Erik Prince adds to the confusion, and repeats the Kirikounews report of a Chadian–Salvadoran quarrel.',evidence='Opinion column',other='',links=[['The column', 'https://www.paololuers.com/columnas/con-bukele-se-agudiza-la-crisis-en-haiti']]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 20:40',who='Nancy Roc (@TheNancyRoc), with Frantz Duval, on RFI',where='Radio France Internationale, French',url='https://x.com/TheNancyRoc/status/2115876346685464809',text='On RFI, Le Nouvelliste\'s editor Frantz Duval says 2,000 Salvadoran soldiers have arrived, that El Salvador is massing troops and equipment with the Haitian government\'s support, that "the legal framework of this deployment remains unclear," and that "the GSF and the UN say nothing."',evidence='Radio interview, named speaker',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 19:57',who='@vargavila, also posted by DerechaDiarioRD',where='X, Gonaïves',url='https://x.com/vargavila/status/2115865726657659048',text='Video in which a man presented as a Gran Grif leader challenges the Salvadorans and the Gang Suppression Force.',evidence='Video, about 8 seconds; the speaker and place are as the posters describe them',other='Not yet reported by others.',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 19:33',who='Rolfy Martínez (@RolfyMartinez)',where='X, Port-au-Prince',url='https://x.com/RolfyMartinez/status/2115859496102932816',text='Video of the combined forces with the Salvadorans clearing barricades and pushing into gang territory, and (16:52) of Salvadoran troops working alongside the Haitian police and the Gang Suppression Force in "vulnerable areas" of Port-au-Prince, with "an advance against the Haitian gangs with more power and more units deployed."',evidence='Videos; places not shown',other='',links=[['Video of Salvadorans with the police and the force', 'https://x.com/RolfyMartinez/status/2115818948629323837']]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 19:25',who='European Union spokesperson (@AnouarEUspox), EU External Action Service',where='X and EEAS statement, Brussels',url='https://x.com/AnouarEUspox/status/2115857483113910395',text='The EU spokesperson\'s statement on Haiti says "credible, transparent and democratic elections are essential" and welcomes the Security Council\'s extension of the Gang Suppression Force\'s mandate, "whose role is crucial." The statement does not mention El Salvador. The Miami Herald says it followed a meeting of diplomats with the Prime Minister.',evidence='Official statement',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 18:32',who='Danny Shaw (@profdannyshaw), US writer on Haiti',where='X, English',url='https://x.com/profdannyshaw/status/2115844285845197127',text='"Where is Barbecue?" Shaw posts video of two of Jimmy Chérizier\'s supporters, Ralph Laurent and Kim Ives, explaining why he has "chosen to stay silent," and argues that Viv Ansanm\'s mission is over and that the foreign troops are there to take over the gangs\' criminal economy.',evidence='Video interview; opinion',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 17:29',who='Noticias SIN, quoting former deputy Vinicio Castillo Semán (FNP)',where='Santo Domingo',url='https://noticiassin.com/pais/nacional/2026/10/29/vinicio-castillo-califica-de-hostil-convocatoria-de-haiti-2157434/',text='Castillo calls Haiti\'s summons of the Dominican ambassador "a hostile act," says the Dominican Republic has given $20 million to the force, and asks the armed forces for a plan in case of a mass exodus. ACD Media quotes Sigfrido Pared Pérez blaming Haitian confusion for the summons.',evidence='Named politicians quoted',other="We found no report on the outcome of the noon meeting at Haiti's foreign ministry.",links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 16:36',who='Dánica Coto, Associated Press, via the Los Angeles Times',where='San Juan, Puerto Rico, on Port-au-Prince',url='https://www.latimes.com/world-nation/story/2026-10-29/haiti-announces-new-election-dates-as-2-000-salvadoran-troops-help-fight-gangs',text='Haiti\'s electoral council set the first round of elections for 18 Jul 2027 and the second for 4 Oct 2027, replacing the 13 Dec date, with voter registration ending 20 May. The story quotes Romain Le Cour on the "opaque" Salvadoran rules of engagement and the role of Vectus, and the Norwegian Refugee Council, two of whose Haitian staff were killed: "Neither the Haitian society nor the outside world can tolerate that civilians, including aid workers, are killed with impunity."',evidence='Electoral council calendar; named people and agencies quoted',other='Another source says voter registration ends 19 May (HaitiInfoProj, via Nouvel Toupatou, 11:32). The Haitian Times says the earlier 30 Aug and 13 Dec dates are scrapped; candidate registration is extended to 15 Nov.',links=[['HaitiInfoProj on the calendar', 'https://x.com/HaitiInfoProj/status/2115738631872680211']]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 16:30',who='Jake Johnston (@JakobJohnston)',where='X, Washington',url='https://x.com/JakobJohnston/status/2115813638388731915',text='"The flights keep coming. Likely more Salvadoran troops on their way to Haiti today. Already at least 2,000 on the ground." Earlier (14:41) he posted video of one of two Honduran charter planes that have ferried troops over the past week; the other charter company is based in Ecuador. "Still unclear who is paying for all this."',evidence='Analyst posts with flight-tracking image and video',other='',links=[['Honduran charter video', 'https://x.com/JakobJohnston/status/2115786096378286356']]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 14:35',who='Merlín Delcid, CNN en Español',where='San Salvador',url='https://cnnespanol.cnn.com/2026/10/29/latinoamerica/el-salvador-2000-soldados-haiti-rescate-orix',text='Salvadorans are divided over the deployment. A driver saw two buses and a truck of soldiers under police escort heading to the airport. One man says the country should not get involved in Haiti; a woman says it is right to bring the soldiers back. Criminologist Misael Rivas Soriano says the troops need intelligence on the ground and interpreters. No Salvadoran casualties and no trace of the four have been reported.',evidence='Named witnesses and an expert',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 14:27',who='Jake Johnston (@JakobJohnston)',where='X, Washington',url='https://x.com/JakobJohnston/status/2115782653282525276',text='Johnston\'s takeaways from the two governments\' statements: more than 2,000 troops are on the ground; this is a bilateral deal, so the two "must have signed a Status of Forces agreement"; "El Salvador doesn\'t even acknowledge the UN-authorized GSF"; and it is "a longer-term deployment well beyond search and rescue."',evidence="Analyst's reading of the official statements",other='Another source says no status-of-forces agreement had been signed (Miami Herald sources).',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 14:24',who='10Noticias, Dominican Republic',where='Santo Domingo',url='https://www.10noticias.com.do/titular/haiti-entrega-a-empresas-extranjeras-vigilancia-fronteriza-onu-advierte/',text="The outlet reviews Haiti's contracts with private firms: Vectus Global's ten-year deal to retake gang territory and later collect customs at the Dominican border for 10 percent of added revenue, and a $542.6 million border-surveillance contract with Evergreen Trading System Limited. It cites UN reports S/2025/642 and the Panel of Experts report of 8 Sep 2026, which calls the security response fragmented.",evidence="UN reports and Prince's earlier CNN interview",other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 13:24',who='Amitié FM (@AmitieFmHaiti), on the Gang Suppression Force',where='X, Port-au-Prince',url='https://x.com/AmitieFmHaiti/status/2115766700645790002',text="The station relays the force's warning against false information about its operations and its call to rely on official channels.",evidence='Statement of the force as relayed',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 13:00',who='Romain Le Cour (@romainlecour), Global Initiative Against Transnational Organized Crime',where='X thread, French and English',url='https://x.com/romainlecour/status/2115760706801062238',text='Le Cour says the situation is at a standstill and civilians are more exposed while the Haitian authorities stay silent. Residents of Santo are trapped between the gangs and heavy weapons and drone strikes; Doctors Without Borders reports civilians killed by gunfire and drones, yet no one has called for a corridor. The deployment is opaque on rules of engagement, command, objectives and duration, and on coordination with the Gang Suppression Force, the police and Vectus. "A single national deployment will surpass the entire multilateral force." He asks why the technicians were in a gang area at all.',evidence="Analyst's thread",other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 12:08',who='Kirikounews (@Kirikounews)',where='X, Port-au-Prince',url='https://x.com/Kirikounews/status/2115747715648836088',text='The outlet says a sharp quarrel broke out between Chadian forces of the Gang Suppression Force and the Salvadoran defense minister, and that the Chadians refuse to help the Salvadorans. It says there is no official word yet. Relayed by JounalRosemonV, Wilson_R38 and Paolo Luers.',evidence='No source named; photo',other='Not yet reported by others.',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 11:44',who='HaitiInfoProj (@HaitiInfoProj)',where='X, Port-au-Prince',url='https://x.com/HaitiInfoProj/status/2115741450725917016',text='Cargo flights continue despite storms. The account says Bukele appears to want part of the Salvadoran command working side by side with the Gang Suppression Force but without its formal authorizations.',evidence='No source given',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 07:14',who='@Dark_Linkz',where='X, lower Artibonite',url='https://x.com/Dark_Linkz/status/2115673732698214859',text='The account says a joint operation of the police BRI unit and the Gang Suppression Force on 28 Oct killed more than ten suspected members of Gran Grif, the gang led by Luckson Élan.',evidence='No source named',other='Not yet reported by others.',links=[]),
