dict(when='2026-10-29 05:16',who='HaitiInfoProj (@HaitiInfoProj)',where='X, San Salvador and Port-au-Prince',url='https://x.com/HaitiInfoProj/status/2115643984131637375',text='"Reports indicate" that Bukele\'s near-term goal is a detachment of 5,000, including two special forces units and at least two more helicopter squadrons.',evidence='Video; no source named',other='Another source says about 2,500 by the end of Thursday (Miami Herald).',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 04:39',who='InnovaNews7 (@InnovaNews7), citing Bertide Horace',where='X, lower Artibonite',url='https://x.com/InnovaNews7/status/2115634492190720108',text='Jean Aladin, a member of a lower Artibonite self-defense brigade who owns the outlet CAMERA LAKAY, was arrested on 27 Oct. His phone held messages with Kenken Cha Dépye, a former brigade member who joined Gran Grif, amid accusations that brigade members work with Gran Grif.',evidence='Named local figure quoted',other='Not yet reported by others.',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 03:55',who='Foreign Ministry of El Salvador (@cancilleriasv) and the Office of the Haitian Prime Minister (@PrimatureHT)',where='X, San Salvador and Port-au-Prince',url='https://x.com/cancilleriasv/status/2115623587608502505',text='President Bukele spoke by phone with Prime Minister Alix Didier Fils-Aimé on the evening of Wed 28 Oct about the operation to rescue the four Salvadoran soldiers. The Salvadoran ministry says Bukele stressed "the forcefulness of the operation, with a deployment of more than 2,000 soldiers" and said El Salvador will keep supporting security work against the gangs in Haiti. The Haitian Prime Minister\'s office put out a communiqué titled "Haïti – El Salvador: renforcement de la coopération sécuritaire" (02:47); as relayed by Radio Métronome and Patriarche Radio, it says the two leaders will strengthen bilateral coordination and operational cooperation "within the framework of the Gang Suppression Force," and insists on cooperation that respects the authority of the Haitian state.',evidence="Official statements from both governments, each with a photo; we read the Haitian communiqué only through the radio stations' summaries (the full text is on Facebook)",other="Another source says the Salvadoran buildup is happening outside the UN mandate for the force (EFE, 28 Oct). Patriarche Radio puts the number deployed at about 2,077 and repeats the Miami Herald's report that a US C-130 flew Salvadoran soldiers in on 23 Oct.",links=[("Haitian Prime Minister's post", 'https://x.com/PrimatureHT/status/2115606389426987462'), ('Radio Métronome', 'https://x.com/Radio_Metronome/status/2115613084165497143'), ('Patriarche Radio', 'https://x.com/PatriarcheRadio/status/2115624174202822737'), ('Le Quotidien 509', 'https://x.com/lequotidien509/status/2115624989806190949')]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 03:37',who='Rolfy Martínez (@RolfyMartinez), Dominican journalist, relaying Lanmò San Jou of 400 Mawozo',where='X, place not shown',url='https://x.com/RolfyMartinez/status/2115618925006196973',text='Video in which the 400 Mawozo leader shows off a pet crocodile. Martínez: "While President Bukele is out looking for him, he is raising his giant lizard."',evidence="Video, about 1 minute 50 seconds, from the gang leader's own social media; no date or place we can check",other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 03:12',who='Magazine Haïti (@maghaiti), citing Diario Libre',where='X, Dominican–Haitian border',url='https://x.com/maghaiti/status/2115612704576553063',text='The Dominican army denies reports of a Haitian gang incursion at the border, calling them "false and malicious," and says border communities are going about their business while troops keep watch. On 26 Oct President Abinader said he would not let Haitian gangs within 20 kilometers of Dominican territory.',evidence='Army statement as relayed; photo',other='Haiti\'s foreign ministry has summoned Dominican Ambassador Faruk Miguel for noon on Thu 29 Oct over reported Dominican army incursions and home demolitions near Thomazeau; Dominican Foreign Minister Víctor "Ito" Bisonó says the ambassador will attend and asks for proof (Le Quotidien 509, RCC Noticias).',links=[('Le Quotidien 509, ambassador summoned', 'https://lequotidien509.com/expulsions-a-thomazeau-raina-forbin-convoque-lambassadeur-dominicain-ito-bisono-exige-des-preuves/')]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 03:10',who='Herbert Esmahan (@HerbertEsmahan), Salvadoran political analyst, on One America News (@OANN)',where='X, TV interview',url='https://x.com/OANN/status/2115612077909999673',text='"President Bukele mentioned that this is a spiritual war that the world is facing, and many of these gangs in Haiti are practitioners of the occult... By commending this mission to God, I believe we will be successful." He says he is confident El Salvador will bring its men home.',evidence='Video clip of a named analyst; opinion',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 00:48',who='Carel Pèdre (@carelpedre), Haitian radio and TV host',where='X, in Creole',url='https://x.com/carelpedre/status/2115576459851080162',text='A timeline of how slow the last foreign help was: Ariel Henry asked for help in October 2022, the UN Security Council authorized the Kenya-led mission in October 2023, and the first Kenyan police arrived on 25 June 2024, nearly 20 months later. Bukele, by contrast, mobilized in a few days. Pèdre grants the two operations have different legal and logistical frames, but says the gap shows the problem "was never only a lack of means" but of political will and leadership. About 8,900 views.',evidence='Commentary with dates; no sources linked',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 00:43',who='Rolfy Martínez (@RolfyMartinez), relaying Lanmò San Jou of 400 Mawozo',where='X, place not shown',url='https://x.com/RolfyMartinez/status/2115575272242102761',text='Video in which a woman asks the 400 Mawozo leader for money; a backpack full of cash is brought and he hands bills to everyone passing by. Martínez: "This guy uses these moments to film and upload them. You judge."',evidence="Video, about 1 minute 30 seconds, filmed by the gang's own people; no date or place we can check",other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 00:41',who='Le Quotidien 509 (@lequotidien509), Haitian online paper',where='X, Santo Domingo',url='https://x.com/lequotidien509/status/2115574581171790088',text='The Dominican government says it has spent more than $21 million supporting the Gang Suppression Force. It is also reinforcing its troops on the border while ruling out any direct intervention on Haitian soil.',evidence='Government figure as reported; we did not open the full article',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-29 00:05',who='Magazine Haïti (@maghaiti)',where='X, Delmas 83, Port-au-Prince',url='https://x.com/maghaiti/status/2115565739939926117',text='Cultural journalist Richard Alexandre Vedette, known as Caonabo, 38, founder of Vedette Mag and formerly of Radio Puissance, Ticket Magazine, Loop Haïti and Sibelle Haïti, was shot dead on Tuesday 27 Oct at Delmas 83. The circumstances are not yet known.',evidence='Named victim, photo; no police statement given',other='Not yet reported by others among the sources we read.',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-28 23:09',who='Rolfy Martínez (@RolfyMartinez), relaying Lanmò San Jou of 400 Mawozo',where='X, place not shown',url='https://x.com/RolfyMartinez/status/2115551644515782796',text='Video of the 400 Mawozo leader walking through what Martínez calls his former mansion, with a pool and a private gym. About 17,000 views.',evidence='Video, about 29 seconds; no date or place we can check',other='Earlier that day (05:07) Martínez posted images of the same man that he says were deleted from the internet in 2024.',links=[('Martínez, older images', 'https://x.com/RolfyMartinez/status/2115279137485050057')]),
dict(when='2026-10-28 22:04',who='Le Quotidien 509 (@lequotidien509)',where='X, Cul-de-Sac plain',url='https://x.com/lequotidien509/status/2115535071050694898',text='The Gang Suppression Force says it will keep up the pressure on the gangs despite what happened to the Salvadoran contingent. In the Cul-de-Sac plain, where operations go on, residents have fled their homes, and others are stuck inside without basic supplies.',evidence='Report with photo; no named residents in the post',other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-28 21:43',who='Jean Garry Denis, opinion piece in Le Nouvelliste',where='Le Nouvelliste website, Port-au-Prince',url='https://lenouvelliste.com/article/273379/lintervention-de-bukele-suite-au-drame-des-militaires-salvadoriens',text='"L\'intervention de Bukele suite au drame des militaires salvadoriens." Denis says Bukele\'s intervention could clear some criminal pockets but cannot bring a lasting solution without breaking the ties between officials and gangs and cutting off arms. He accuses Prime Minister Fils-Aimé of hiring Erik Prince\'s Vectus Global and renewing "an opaque contract" worth $52 million, of taking more than three days to react after 18 Oct, and of flying to Mexico by private jet while Salvadoran troops landed "without any legal framework." He cites the UN finding that more than 900,000 items, mostly ammunition, were diverted from Dominican police stocks to Haiti.',evidence="Signed opinion piece; the $52 million and jet figures are the author's, without documents",other='',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-28 20:32',who='EFE (Spanish news agency), via Infobae and El Diario de Hoy',where='Port-au-Prince',url='https://www.infobae.com/america/agencias/2026/10/28/el-salvador-despliega-unos-1300-soldados-en-haiti-para-hacer-frente-a-las-pandillas/',text='EFE says the Salvadoran deployment "is taking place outside the mandate defined in September 2025 by the UN Security Council" for the Gang Suppression Force. It quotes Le Nouvelliste\'s government source: "The government prefers to stay quiet and act." EFE says the contingent, which includes special forces, is the largest any one country has sent to Haiti since the UN mission MINUSTAH left in 2017, and that more charter flights are expected.',evidence='Agency report; government source not named',other='Another source says the cooperation is "within the framework" of the force (Haitian Prime Minister\'s communiqué, 29 Oct). Rezo Nodwes built a long thread on the EFE point (23:21).',links=[('El Diario de Hoy', 'https://www.elsalvador.com/noticias/nacional/soldados-salvadorenos-desplegados-haiti/1301094/2026/'), ('Rezo Nodwes', 'https://x.com/rezo_nodwes/status/2115554492641091882')]),
dict(when='2026-10-28 20:26',who='Rolfy Martínez (@RolfyMartinez)',where='X, Carrefour-Feuilles, Port-au-Prince',url='https://x.com/RolfyMartinez/status/2115510620816621936',text='Video he says shows the "united forces" with Haiti forcing their way through the streets of Carrefour-Feuilles, which the gangs had blocked to keep the Haitian police out. About 84,000 views.',evidence="Video, about 48 seconds; Martínez's description; no date or place shown that we can check",other='Not yet reported by others among the sources we read.',links=[]),
dict(when='2026-10-28 19:35',who='Jake Johnston (@JakobJohnston), Haiti analyst at CEPR',where='X',url='https://x.com/JakobJohnston/status/2115497683670450240',text='"Two flights from El Salvador have already landed today and two more are scheduled. There could easily be some 2,000 troops on the ground by the end of the day, though it\'s possible these flights are bringing additional equipment instead. Still, the expectation is at least 3,000 troops will eventually deploy."',evidence='Named analyst; flight listings; no source given for the 3,000',other='Lune Actus (Creole) also says El Salvador could go as high as 3,000.',links=[('Lune Actus', 'https://x.com/LuneActus/status/2115622229903913088')]),
dict(when='2026-10-28 19:34',who='@MkubwaGlobal, Africa commentary account',where='X, English',url='https://x.com/MkubwaGlobal/status/2115497448734965790',text='A long post linking Erik Prince\'s contractors in Congo to Haiti: it says about 20 of his contractors were killed or wounded in an ambush in eastern Congo on 17 Sep, notes that the US Treasury sanctioned Rwanda\'s Ministry of Defence on 28 Oct over M23, and warns against carrying "the Haiti surge model" to Africa. It says no public evidence links the sanctions to the ambush.',evidence='Commentary; cites Reuters and the Treasury notice without links we could open',other='Prince reposted news of the Rwanda sanctions on 28 Oct; he posted nothing about Haiti.',links=[]),
