dict(when='2026-10-28 18:35',who='Doctors Without Borders (MSF), quoted by Jake Johnston (@JakobJohnston)',where='MSF website and X, Port-au-Prince',url='https://www.doctorswithoutborders.org/latest/civilians-and-medical-facilities-must-be-spared-amid-surging-violence-haiti',text='Between 18 and 26 Oct, 30 people hurt by gunfire or drone attacks were treated at MSF hospitals in Tabarre and Cité Soleil, including women and children. Since 18 Oct "heavy gunfire and drone strikes have increased in the Plaine du Cul-de-Sac." Head of mission Davina Hayles: "We fear that this armed conflict will claim even more victims and displace even more people in the coming days, particularly with the arrival of additional international security forces." Some patients took hours to reach care because roads and bridges are blocked; some MSF staff have fled their homes and are sheltering at MSF sites.',evidence='Named official, photos',other='',links=[("Johnston's post", 'https://x.com/JakobJohnston/status/2115482574881431729')]),
