dict(when='2026-10-28 14:22',who='Stéphane Eustache, op-ed shared by Haiti Info Project (@HaitiInfoProj)',where='X, English',url='https://x.com/HaitiInfoProj/status/2115418969549201489',text='"Bukele\'s Ambition for Military Autonomy in the Face of International Law Requirements" (Kreyol Press Dessalines). Eustache argues Bukele cannot decide alone that his troops will run their own armed operations in Haiti: the Gang Suppression Force works under a Security Council authorization, and a separate operation would need its own legal basis, Haiti\'s consent and clear coordination. He warns that rival chains of command could weaken the fight against the gangs and blur who answers for harm to civilians.',evidence='Signed opinion piece',other='',links=[]),
