dict(when='2026-10-27 19:56',who='Reuters (via The Straits Times and CBC)',where='Port-au-Prince and San Salvador',url='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/around-1000-soldiers-from-el-salvador-have-deployed-to-haiti-source-says',text='About 1,000 Salvadoran soldiers have deployed to Haiti, says a security official in Haiti who asked not to be named. It is unclear who commands them or how long they will stay. A US military official says Southern Command C-130s helped move them; flight-tracking shows the flights, and a lawmaker from Bukele\'s party posted a photo of soldiers on a plane. The Gang Suppression Force has about 2,000 personnel, a third of its planned strength; before the ambush there were at least 124 Salvadorans. Pierre Espérance (RNDDH, a Haitian rights group) welcomed the troops but warned: "Not everybody living in gang-controlled areas are gangsters." Wilson Joseph of 400 Mawozo denies holding the men. Analyst Luis Contreras expects some troops to work outside the force\'s chain of command, coordinating with Erik Prince\'s company.',evidence='Anonymous security official and unnamed US military official; named analyst and rights advocate; flight-tracking data',other='El Español (Spain) adds that direct flights by the Ecuadorian airline Aeroregional carried troops; Radio Télé Galaxie and other Haitian outlets relayed the 1,000 figure in French and Creole.',links=[('CBC', 'https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/el-salvador-soldiers-deployed-haiti-9.7398494'), ('El Español', 'https://www.elespanol.com/mundo/20261027/bukele-despliega-soldados-haiti-desaparicion-militares-salvadorenos-combatian-pandillas/1003744437401_0.html')]),
